      "name": "Concept",
      "names": {"uk":"Концепція"},
      "status": "concept",
      "description": "An unofficial concept, not a city plan: three lines through the centre and a ring. The Prutska line runs west to east from Rosha to Hraviton, the Sadhirsko-Pivdenna line from Sadhora south across the centre, with a branch west through Pivdennyi Masyv to Barcelona, and the Holovna line along the main street from the Prut to Pivdenna; the Kiltseva ring links the station, the airport and the south. Chernivtsi has never planned a metro; the stations stand, roughly, on the places they are named after.",
